+    // Execute the trace function without capture to compile programs and
+    // populate program cache. Twice: an op's first run can leave a persistent
+    // allocation (e.g. a collective's global semaphore in L1), and ops whose
+    // program depends on free L1, such as a matmul's block sizes, would then
+    // need a different program during capture than in the first warmup, if
+    // they run before it. The second warmup compiles them as captured.
+    for (int warmup = 0; warmup < 2; ++warmup) {
+      builder.create<func::CallOp>(captureFunc.getLoc(), traceFunc,
+                                   warmupArgs);
+    }
 
